# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_coverage_percent.py" "COVERAGE PERCENT GATE: PASS" "coverage percent" "coverage-nudge %-only (PO 2026-06-19 'show users only %'): the billing-coverage upgrade nudge appended to a PR check summary shows a COVERAGE PERCENTAGE (how much of the codebase is watched / how full the plan is) — never the raw analyzed-file/Unit count, the plan limit, or the internal billing metric (those stay private; the metric/graph is the moat, the customer-facing magnitude is a %). Proves: OVER the plan -> 'covering ~X%' with no raw count/limit; NEAR -> 'at ~X%'; under-the-line / unlimited paid (file_limit None) / garbled / non-dict -> None (never nudge a payer, never crash); and the rendered line never contains the raw file_count/file_limit nor 'analyzed files'. Offline, no Postgres, pure render" "coverage nudge shows % only (no raw file/Unit count or limit leaked; never nudges a payer; never crashes)" 10
